title: $:/plugins/rimir/outline/readme

! Outline

Work on an ordinary tiddler like on a Streams outline: select a block, edit it in place, move it with Alt-Up/Down, indent it with Tab, and see the result rendered at once. The tiddler stays one tiddler; no helper tiddlers are created.

!! Features

* ''Toggle per tiddler'' — an //outline// button in the view toolbar. Off means the normal view, with no extra handlers.
* ''Same rendering'' — the tiddler renders exactly as usual. Outline mode only adds data attributes, a selection frame and key handling.
* ''Units'' — list items, lists, headings (with their sections), paragraphs, code blocks, tables, opened HTML containers, transclusion lines, and widgets or macro calls (one opaque unit each).
* ''Type badges'' — a small, faint label next to every unit shows what it is (paragraph, h2, code-block, bullet, ...), also on the editor field; they take no space. Settings: all (default), headings only, off.
* ''Selection'' — click, Up/Down in document order, Left/Right to the parent / first child, Escape clears.
* ''Move'' — Alt-Up/Alt-Down swap a unit with its sibling, carrying its subtree. Headings and blocks also move across heading lines: a new heading moves up over the blocks above it, a paragraph moves into the next section.
* ''Indent'' — Tab/Shift-Tab demote/promote list items (one marker character) and headings (one `!`) with their subtrees.
* ''In-place editor'' — Enter or a double-click opens TW's own edit widget at the unit (AutoComplete and other editor plugins work): a compact one-line field by default, optionally the full editor with toolbar. Lists and headings are edited without their marker; nesting stays with Tab/Shift-Tab. Ctrl-Enter saves, Enter saves and starts a new unit, Escape discards, Ctrl-Up/Down save and move the editor to the previous/next unit, Alt-Enter turns the unit into another type. In selection mode Ctrl-Enter starts a new empty unit below the selection.
* ''Delete'' — the Delete key removes the selection with everything below it, after a small yes/no menu (a heading: with its section or just the heading); list items without sub-items go at once (a setting).
* ''Copy, cut, paste'' — Ctrl-C, Ctrl-X, Ctrl-V move a unit with its subtree, also to another tiddler; through the system clipboard: formatted into e-mail or Jira, as wikitext into text fields; pasted into an outline a unit takes the level of the place.
* ''Undo'' — Ctrl-Z takes back the last changes made in the outline (deletes, moves, merges, splits, edits), Ctrl-Y redoes them; for the running session. In the editor too, as long as nothing is typed (after a split, merge or move from the editor).
* ''Split and merge'' — Enter in the middle of a list item splits it at the caret, at the start of a filled item or paragraph it opens an empty one above; Backspace at the start of an item joins it to the item above (an empty item is deleted), Delete at its end pulls the item below up, like in Streams.
* ''Block menu'' — Alt-Enter (also in the editor, to turn the edited unit into another type): insert a new paragraph, heading, list, quote or code block after or before the selection (in an empty tiddler: the first block), or turn the selection into another type (a bullet list into a numbered one, a paragraph into a heading, ...).
* ''Key overview'' — press `?` in an outline (or its small ? button) for a table of all keys; the //keys// tab shows the same. Every key is configurable in the settings tab with TW's shortcut editor.
* ''Transclusions'' — a small marker on `{{…}}` lines; Enter opens the target in outline mode.
* ''Safe writes'' — every write is a splice of a known range; if the text changed underneath, the edit is relocated or refused, never guessed.

!! Prerequisites

* TiddlyWiki 5.4.0 or later (JS modules: server restart or reload needed after install)
* Optional: `rimir/theme` (`rr-` styles in settings), `rimir/doc-template` (branded docs)

!! Quick Start

# Install the plugin and restart the server (the widget and key modules load only at startup).
# Open a wikitext tiddler and press //outline// in its view toolbar.
# Click a block. Move with Up/Down, press Alt-Down to move it below its sibling, Tab to indent it.
# Press Enter, change the text, press Ctrl-Enter to save.
# Press `?` to see all keys.

Wikitext only; Markdown tiddlers are not supported yet.
